                <pb facs="0483" n="409" sameAs="frus:frus1941-43/pg409"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hopkins Papers</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Minister of Supply</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Beaverbrook</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Presidents Special Assistant</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hopkins</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-01-01">January 1,
                        1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Harry</hi>, Cables &amp; Wireless will agree
                    to the proposals for prohibiting transmissions by wireless from South America to
                    Italy and Tokyo.</p>
                <p>Cables &amp; Wireless warn me that diplomatic action in South America will be
                    necessary, as the services there are controlled by local companies.</p>
                <p>I am getting a cable on the subject tomorrow and I will then write another
                    letter.</p>
                <p>Yours ever,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Max</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
